WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.242
Hi, I'm Kiwi!

00:00:02.242 --> 00:00:05.417
Decision models like Jev pick an answer without writing one.

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:06.052
Here's how.

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:12.466
If the answers form a fixed list, don't type one out.

00:00:12.466 --> 00:00:14.397
Prefill once, and read each option's score.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.093
The usual way: the model types its answer, one token at a time.

00:00:22.513 --> 00:00:26.678
The scoring way: prefill once, generate nothing, and read the log-probabilities

00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:28.193
of the option tokens.

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:30.229
The best-scored option wins.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:33.864
SGLang has served exactly this since June twenty twenty-five.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:39.278
One readout lists the options as letters and reads them from one position.

00:00:39.278 --> 00:00:43.406
That brings a slot bias: A is worth one point seven one logits.

00:00:43.826 --> 00:00:48.529
The other gives each candidate its own branch, and sums its tokens' log-probabilities.

00:00:48.529 --> 00:00:51.062
No order bias, a length bias instead.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.034
A search has three jobs.

00:00:54.034 --> 00:00:58.107
First, enumerate: the harness lists the moves, and picks how wide to branch.

00:00:58.527 --> 00:01:02.665
Second, price: the model scores every branch over one shared prefill, so

00:01:02.665 --> 00:01:04.044
width is almost free.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.326
Third, sequence, and nobody holds it.

00:01:06.326 --> 00:01:09.739
Each level is a fresh call that re-reads the state, so

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:10.980
depth is what costs.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:16.410
On two hundred and twenty hard items, two untrained decoders beat

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.965
every trained small encoder.

00:01:17.965 --> 00:01:21.853
Laya, which beat Jev at home, lands eighty-eight items behind.

00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:26.122
The readout is a serving feature, not a model feature.

00:01:26.122 --> 00:01:29.310
Pricing is the model's job; planning lives in the harness.

00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:35.352
To recap: score, don't decode; two readouts; and a model that prices

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:36.698
while the harness plans.

00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:39.254
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:39.864
I'm Kiwi.

00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:40.169
Bye!
